This project is and remains **open source under the MIT License**. It is the MCP server,
Roll20 Mod relay and D&D Beyond read bridge for AI-assisted D&D 5e session management.

The gem moved out; the server did not
------------------------------------

Until 2026-08-11 this repository also contained `voice-hud/` — the Electron voice HUD known
as **DM Whisper**. On that date it was extracted into its own repository
(https://github.com/eschatus/dm-whisper) with `git subtree split`, preserving all commits,
authors and dates, and its source was closed.

**Only the gem closed. This repository stays open**, and DM Whisper consumes it as an
ordinary dependency. Nothing here became proprietary, and nothing here is encumbered by the
gem's terms.

If you are looking for code that used to be under `voice-hud/`, its history is intact in the
other repository. Copies of it obtained from this repository before 2026-08-11 were obtained
under the licence declared at the time and remain governed by it — see that project's NOTICE.

Licence history
---------------

From the first commit (2026-05-25) until 2026-08-11 this repository declared
`"license": "ISC"` in package.json and carried no LICENSE file. That was a real, public,
permissive grant, and copies obtained under it remain licensed under ISC.

The LICENSE file added on 2026-08-11 states MIT. ISC and MIT are equivalent in substance —
both permit use, modification and redistribution with the notice retained — so this records
what was already true rather than changing what anyone may do. It was done because a
permissive intention that exists only as a package.json field is not a licence anybody should
have to rely on.

